From: Codex <codex@openai.com>
Subject: [PATCH] hwsim: refresh frame registrations during wiphy reconfigure

nl80211_update_wiphy() has a second AP stop/start lifecycle which does not use
restart_interface().  It stops every active BSS, deinitializes embedded
hostapd, and later calls start_bss(), but it leaves the management-frame and
EAPOL receive sockets associated with the stopped hwsim BSS.

The result is a band-specific half-working AP after a radio update: the kernel
continues to beacon and the station can scan the BSS, but Open System
Authentication requests never reach embedded hostapd and the station times
out.  Restarting OneWifi restores the sockets and makes the same station and
RF matrix associate immediately.

Release the old receive paths before STOP_AP in this reconfiguration path.
start_bss() then creates one fresh set through wifi_drv_set_operstate(), just
as it does in the restart_interface() lifecycle fixed separately.  Keep this
hwsim-only so physical drivers retain their native registration behavior.

Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 wifi_hal_nl80211.c | 16 ++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 16 insertions(+)

diff --git a/wifi_hal_nl80211.c b/wifi_hal_nl80211.c
index 6d5cf2f..6fe5149 100644
--- a/wifi_hal_nl80211.c
+++ b/wifi_hal_nl80211.c
@@ -8343,6 +8343,22 @@ int nl80211_update_wiphy(wifi_radio_info_t *radio)
     while (interface != NULL) {
         if (interface->bss_started) {
                 reconfigure = true;
+#ifdef HWSIM_RADIO
+                /* nl80211_update_wiphy() owns an AP stop/start path which
+                 * bypasses restart_interface().  Registrations attached to
+                 * the stopped hwsim BSS must be released before start_bss()
+                 * creates their replacements.  Retaining them leaves a BSS
+                 * that beacons but never receives authentication frames. */
+                if (interface->mgmt_frames_registered) {
+                    nl80211_unregister_mgmt_frames(interface);
+                }
+#ifndef EAPOL_OVER_NL
+                if (interface->data_frames_registered) {
+                    unregister_data_frame_socket(interface);
+                }
+#endif /* EAPOL_OVER_NL */
+#endif /* HWSIM_RADIO */
+
                 nl80211_enable_ap(interface, false);
                 pthread_mutex_lock(&g_wifi_hal.hapd_lock);
                 deinit_bss(&interface->u.ap.hapd);
